**/target
.git
*.log
# Security review 2026-07-27: core/Dockerfile's build stage does `COPY . .`
# (whole build context) before `mvn package` - without these exclusions,
# core/.env.local (APP_ENCRYPTION_KEY, KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_SECRET, etc. - see
# this repo's root CLAUDE.md Rule 0) gets copied straight into the build
# stage's image layer even though the runtime stage only COPYs the built
# jar out of it. That layer is still recoverable (docker build --target
# build, or any exported/pushed build cache) - .env.local was never meant
# to leave the host. web/.dockerignore and web-admin/.dockerignore already
# excluded the equivalent file; core's did not.
.env
.env.*
.env.local
# Editor / tooling droppings and any stray JS installs never belong in the build context.
**/node_modules
**/.idea
**/.vscode
